render-file id sets (after-receipt-5 research package 3, 28 Sep 2026). Read-only; loose trees (R53 roots) + the committed anchors.
Per title and family:
  T   thumbnail ids (file names; strays of another prefix in the folder reported), SHA-256 per package -> byte-identical duplicate groups;
  V   the stored values of the DB column (anchor DB), distinct + per-value row counts; mask also the team slots (exhibitionteams
      goaliemask<k>_{starter,backup}, non-zero);
  S   shift discriminator: |{v + k : v in V} & T| / |V| for k = -2 .. +2 (a numeric-filename candidate must fit at exactly one k);
  R   every render prefix / numeric position (`rendering/<fam>` and `rendering/fe<fam>`) set P: |T & P|, T == P, T <= P, P <= T;
  X   V - T (stored values with no thumbnail at the best shift) and T - V counts.
This is file-NAME evidence (a numeric-filename candidate), not a data edge: no table joining values to thumbnails was found (see handoff 11).
Usage: python r143_gen7_createplayer_thumbnails.py <r53.json> <out.json>
